The table shows $5$ students' height and arm span. The scatter plot below is missing one of the $5$ points.
$\begin{array}{c|ccccc} \text{Student} & \text{Omar} & \text{Pia} & \text{Qing} & \text{Rhea} & \text{Sam} \\ \hline \text{Height (cm)} & 152.5 & 162.5 & 172.5 & 180 & 190 \\ \text{Arm span (cm)} & 157.5 & 150 & 182.5 & 170 & 185 \end{array}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.68]
\draw[gray!25,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=1] (0,0) grid (10,10);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,0) -- (10.6,0);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,0) -- (0,11.6);
\foreach \x/\lbl in {0/145,2/155,4/165,6/175,8/185,10/195} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\lbl$};}
\foreach \y/\lbl in {0/145,2/155,4/165,6/175,8/185,10/195} {\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,\y) {$\lbl$};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.8,5) {Arm span (cm)};
\node[below] at (5,-1.1) {Height (cm)};
\node at (5,11.1) {Height vs arm span};
\fill (1.5,2.5) circle (2.2pt);
\fill (3.5,1) circle (2.2pt);
\fill (7,5) circle (2.2pt);
\fill (9,8) circle (2.2pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which height and arm span is the missing point (Qing's) at?

The scatter plot below shows $4$ students' height and arm span. A new student, Farid, has height $170$ cm and arm span $180$ cm. Four candidate positions, $A$ to $D$, are marked.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.68]
\draw[gray!25,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=1] (0,0) grid (10,10);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,0) -- (10.6,0);
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,0) -- (0,11.6);
\foreach \x/\lbl in {0/145,2/155,4/165,6/175,8/185,10/195} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\lbl$};}
\foreach \y/\lbl in {0/145,2/155,4/165,6/175,8/185,10/195} {\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,\y) {$\lbl$};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.8,5) {Arm span (cm)};
\node[below] at (5,-1.1) {Height (cm)};
\node at (5,11.1) {Height vs arm span};
\fill (2,1) circle (2.2pt);
\fill (4,3) circle (2.2pt);
\fill (6,8) circle (2.2pt);
\fill (8,6) circle (2.2pt);
\node[above right,font=\footnotesize] at (5,7) {$A$};\fill (5,7) circle (2.2pt);
\node[above right,font=\footnotesize] at (7,5) {$B$};\fill (7,5) circle (2.2pt);
\node[above right,font=\footnotesize] at (5,6) {$C$};\fill (5,6) circle (2.2pt);
\node[above left,font=\footnotesize] at (4,7) {$D$};\fill (4,7) circle (2.2pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which position is where Farid's point should be plotted?

